      "writtenOn": "2026-01-12T06:16:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this the mechanism to disallow `MapAsync` And Queue\u0027s operations from using the buffer concurrently?\n\nI\u0027m thinking maybe it would be generalized to apply to all object types. Would a simpler boolean flag `ApiObjectBase::mExclusiveUse` work? We could use atomic CAS to allow only 1 thread to set it to true and proceed, the other threads would fail and return validation error.\n\nFor example, this could be applied to prevent `Queue.Submit` \u0026 `Destroy` from using the an object simultaneously. I think it\u0027s also useful for many other methods we want to avoid concurrent use in future.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 141,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 141,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "b1e9071ca6556e5c0877f4778b38bd19840b4543",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e7ba9e83_040f00df",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/Buffer.h",
